{"id": "EUVD-2026-82233", "enisaUuid": "48508d21-16f6-3d11-8d64-37b7b4f66475", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Reject rdonly/rdwr_buf_size kfunc arguments that exceed u32 max\n\ncheck_kfunc_args() detects a kfunc argument named rdonly_buf_size or\nrdwr_buf_size and stores reg->var_off.value into meta->r0_size, a u64,\nand does not bound it. check_kfunc_call() later copies that value into\nthe returned register's mem_size field:\n\n  meta->r0_size = reg->var_off.value;\n  ...\n  regs[BPF_REG_0].mem_size = meta.r0_size;\n\nregs[BPF_REG_0].mem_size is u32. A constant whose upper 32 bits are set\ngets truncated instead of causing a load-time rejection, so the verifier\nrecords a PTR_TO_MEM register with an approximately 4 GiB mem_size for\nwhatever allocation the kfunc returned. A later access check against\nthat register uses the truncated, wrong bound.\n\nReject rdonly_buf_size/rdwr_buf_size values that exceed U32_MAX at the\npoint meta->r0_size is set.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:11:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:58", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2147065d3a4e1d5d42ae553fef165f17ec5e0e79", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b6ac0b5732047d43172b9dfbe6b57b9b8de303c2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/93a20b14f8627b2d3486e3ec1d3f2e7275a506ec", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/56a3846830ac95a472297d0cbba75cbff29540bb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2aaf67f0516fde29620d0edfc29c01b9ea7ad430"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93125", "GHSA-vqq3-2x9h-9pmg"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "03050e2b-9955-3350-82e8-c50ab5a2321a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eb1f7f71c126c8fd50ea81af98f97c4b581ea4ae <2147065d3a4e1d5d42ae553fef165f17ec5e0e79"}, {"id": "110293a0-8fae-3339-bc29-b0deff36b6fe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "21d06662-9727-3bdc-97d0-92fd961700b3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "44561f9b-322e-373e-931f-5828ddcd4592", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eb1f7f71c126c8fd50ea81af98f97c4b581ea4ae <56a3846830ac95a472297d0cbba75cbff29540bb"}, {"id": "48f8cfd3-b3ce-334b-981a-5974765f737e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "4f3b4211-b37c-37a5-9106-dc94ecef754c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eb1f7f71c126c8fd50ea81af98f97c4b581ea4ae <b6ac0b5732047d43172b9dfbe6b57b9b8de303c2"}, {"id": "8e1193ad-8236-3eab-9e9c-03d9dfeec631", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eb1f7f71c126c8fd50ea81af98f97c4b581ea4ae <93a20b14f8627b2d3486e3ec1d3f2e7275a506ec"}, {"id": "aa35c8f4-11a1-319a-a341-937ce0b3c482", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eb1f7f71c126c8fd50ea81af98f97c4b581ea4ae <2aaf67f0516fde29620d0edfc29c01b9ea7ad430"}, {"id": "b43f96d0-f46e-3693-b8d0-e40b8e03325b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "b8ab8b5f-a96d-3499-982c-9dbffd90917a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1"}, {"id": "e9f69a4d-e7b9-3a01-bed0-b46ec5f33ae1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "f4c126ea-6534-371f-ae87-d3561919035e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "587ecb2a-83ff-325a-8c6f-430242aad0b3", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}